      // [src_eg_worldhistory, src_eg_blain, src_eg_musicweb | 1868-1901 | biography + music-press feature + critic review] The Peer Gynt premiere was praised for its originality (Blain); the biography and a reviewer describe a distinctive style built on Norwegian folk idiom (Slatter from Hardanger fiddle tunes) and a gift for the miniature, while also noting that critics call his range narrow, quote Debussy's 'bonbons wrapped in snow' and say the folk borrowing may be overstated. SELF-CALIBRATION (agent): first-pass 66 / 0.55 lowered to 62 / 0.50 because the originality claims are retrospective and contested within the sources themselves.
