      // [src_frobel_manning, src_frobel_commonplay, src_frobel_britannica | 1816-1840 | education journal + trade article + encyclopaedia] Manning describes a 'structured sequence' of gifts and occupations with step-by-step procedures built on the unity of creation; Community Playthings says his years classifying crystals at the Berlin museum bolstered his belief that fixed laws govern both nature and the child's development, and describes the progression from solids to surfaces, lines and points; Britannica notes his belief in the underlying unity of all things. Consistent with building an ordered system from a general principle, but the crystal link comes from one partisan trade article and the 'unity' idea is a philosophical stance, so the score is modest.
