      experimentation: [74, 0.58, "d", "A"],
      // [src_bose_ieee, src_bose_ijpp, src_bose_scroll | 1895-1920s | institution + review + press] Original components and the idea that no sharp boundary divides living and non-living response; the Dasgupta review nevertheless calls the early radio priority claims parochial and the middle-phase thesis based on a questionable assumption, and the Scroll notes Lodge's earlier demonstration, so the originality is real but uneven and partly rejected.
      creative_originality: [74, 0.62, "d", "D"],
      // [src_bose_ijpp, src_bose_scroll, src_bose_live | 1900-1920 | review + press] After physiologists resisted and some papers were 'archived' by the Royal Society, he was 'undeterred by criticism and isolation', wrote a series of books instead of papers, and kept up plant physiology for about three decades; Live History India says hostility strengthened his resolve. Read from reviews and popular features, not from his own papers, so strong inference.
      persistence: [72, 0.6, "s", "A"],
      // [src_bose_live, src_bose_ijpp, src_bose_scroll | 1900-1920 | press + review] He argued explicitly in Paris in 1900 that lines between the physical and the physiological were arbitrary, against the physiology of his day, and the Scroll says his interpretations even contradicted Darwin's natural selection. Reviewers present this as both his boldness and a weakness, hence dual-edged.
